@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Introduction to Infrastructure as Code (IaC)";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="lead text-center">Learn how Infrastructure as Code (IaC) automates cloud infrastructure management efficiently.</p>
    <hr />

    <!-- What is Infrastructure as Code? -->
    <div class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="text-success">What is Infrastructure as Code?</h2>
        <p>
            Infrastructure as Code (IaC) is the practice of managing and provisioning computing infrastructure through
            machine-readable configuration files instead of manual processes. It allows for automation, consistency,
            and scalability of infrastructure deployment.
        </p>
        <p>
            With IaC, developers and operations teams can define infrastructure using code, making it easier to
            replicate environments and enforce best practices.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/iac-overview.jpg" alt="Infrastructure as Code Overview" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>IaC enables efficient and automated cloud infrastructure management.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Benefits of IaC -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-warning">Benefits of Infrastructure as Code</h2>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Automation:</strong> Reduces manual errors and speeds up deployments.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Consistency:</strong> Ensures identical infrastructure across different environments.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Scalability:</strong> Easily scale resources up or down based on demand.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Version Control:</strong> Infrastructure configurations can be stored in version control systems like Git.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Cost Efficiency:</strong> Optimizes resource usage and reduces operational costs.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/iac-benefits.jpg" alt="Benefits of IaC" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>IaC brings consistency, automation, and cost savings to cloud infrastructure.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Common IaC Tools -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-danger">Common IaC Tools</h2>
        <p>There are several Infrastructure as Code tools available, including:</p>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Terraform:</strong> A popular open-source IaC tool that supports multiple cloud providers.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Azure Resource Manager (ARM) Templates:</strong> Used for defining Azure resources declaratively.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Ansible:</strong> A configuration management tool with IaC capabilities.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Pulumi:</strong> Enables infrastructure management using programming languages like Python, TypeScript, and Go.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>CloudFormation:</strong> AWS's native IaC tool for managing resources.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/iac-tools.jpg" alt="Common IaC Tools" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Popular Infrastructure as Code tools for automating cloud resources.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Best Practices -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-info">Best Practices for IaC</h2>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Use Version Control:</strong> Store all infrastructure code in Git or similar version control systems.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Modularize Code:</strong> Break down configurations into reusable modules.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Implement Security Measures:</strong> Ensure secrets and sensitive data are stored securely.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Test Configurations:</strong> Use automated testing to validate infrastructure changes.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Follow the Principle of Least Privilege:</strong> Minimize permissions for increased security.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/iac-best-practices.jpg" alt="IaC Best Practices" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Following best practices ensures secure and efficient IaC implementations.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Conclusion -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-secondary">Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Infrastructure as Code (IaC) revolutionizes infrastructure management by enabling automation, consistency, and rapid deployment.
            By leveraging tools like Terraform, ARM templates, and Ansible, organizations can efficiently manage cloud resources at scale.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/iac-summary.jpg" alt="IaC Summary" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>IaC helps organizations achieve scalability, automation, and efficiency.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>